// Base condition below is what sigma-cli generates directly from the Sigma
// rule. The aggregation (same account, two or more distinct countries,
// short window) is added by hand here — same gap and same reason as
// password-spray.kql, Sigma's single-rule spec has no clean way to express
// "distinct count of X grouped by Y over a timeframe". This aggregation
// layer didn't exist here for a while — the query matched every successful
// sign-in with no velocity logic at all, only caught by actually running
// the query against synthetic data (see execution-verification/) rather
// than just syntax-checking it.
SigninLogs
| where ResultType == 0
| summarize
    Countries = make_set(Location, 5),
    CountryCount = dcount(Location)
    by UserPrincipalName, bin(TimeGenerated, 30m)
| where CountryCount >= 2   // tune window/threshold against your own traffic before enabling
